DESCRIPTION:Status: turned_in\nClass: 0403_13102Y_Honors Biology-0012_2627
 \nChoose TWO of the four questions to answer based on the documentary ser
 ies Lion.  Your responses should include specific examples from the serie
 s and make direct connections to what we have learned in class.  Each res
 ponse should be 4-6 sentences in length.  You should use proper grammar\,
  capitalization and punctuation.  This is an individual assignment and th
 e use of AI on this assignment in prohibited.  \n\n* Adaptation & Surviva
 l\n\nThe documentary follows lions navigating threats like drought\, prey
  scarcity\, and rival prides. What physical and behavioral adaptive trait
 s do lions have that help them survive in their environment\, and how do 
 these traits reflect natural selection at work in real time?\n\n* Social 
 Structure & Evolutionary Advantage\n\nLions are unique among big cats for
  living in social groups. Based on what you observed\, why might group li
 ving have evolved as an advantageous strategy for lions specifically\, an
 d what biological trade-offs (downsides) come with living in close \nhttp
 s://bcpss.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course_46327&month=09
 &year=2026#assignment_2423018
