SUMMARY:✓ HW: 10/01 Activity Theme Park Access (AP Computer Science Princi
 ples_SY26-27)
DESCRIPTION:Status: turned_in\nClass: AP Computer Science Principles_SY26-
 27\nActivity -  Theme Part Access\n\nYou will create an app that determin
 es a persons access based on:\n\nHeight → Age → Adult supervision\n\nThen
  rewrite one nested solution as a compound Boolean expression.\n\nThe pla
 nning document specifically emphasizes that nested versus compound struct
 ures can both be valid designs and students should compare them for reada
 bility.\n\nYour goal: Create a Python app that decides whether a person c
 an ride an attraction by checking height → age → adult supervision. Then 
 rewrite your nested solution using a compound Boolean expression.\n\nRide
  Rules\n----------\n\nUse these fictional rules for this activity:\n\n*\n
 \nRiders must be at least 48 inches tall.\n\n*\n\nRiders who meet the hei
 ght requirement and are 12 or older may ride without an adult.\n\n*\n\nRi
 ders who meet the height requirement but are under 12 need adult supervis
 ion.\n\nDirections\n----------\n\n*\n\nOpen your Python editor and create
  a file named theme_park_access.py.\n\n*\n\nAsk the user to enter their h
 eight in inches and \nhttps://bcpss.instructure.com/calendar?include_cont
 exts=course_46019&month=10&year=2026#assignment_2433016
